# School topics: {event} the label ("the sports festival"), {eventline} with the day, {school} event/council/project.

@rule me.school
on me.school
- [What do you think about {event}?|Are you ready for {event}?|So, {event}...]
- [How do you feel about {event}?|{Event} is coming, huh?] [Any thoughts?|Got plans?]
- [Heard anything about {event}?|You doing anything for {event}?]

@rule me.school.event
on me.school
when school=event
- [Are you going to {event}?|{Event} is coming up, huh?|Got plans for {event}?]
- [Will you be at {event}?|What are you doing for {event}?|Excited about {event}?]
- [Who are you going to {event} with?|Is {event} worth going to?]

@rule school.plain
on school
opens ask,invite,share
- [{Event}? I haven't thought about it much.|Oh, {event}.] [Should be interesting.|Everyone's talking about it.]
- [{Event}, huh?|Ah, right, {event}.] [I'll go if my friends do.|Could be fun.|It sneaks up every year.]
- [Hmm, {event}.|{Event}? Already?] [I should probably prepare something.|Time flies.]

@rule school.event.cheer
on school
when school=event mood=cheerful|flirty|none
opens invite,ask,tease
feel smile
- [I can't wait for {event}!|{Event}? I've been looking forward to it.] [It's {eventline}, right?|We should go together.|I'm already planning what to wear.]
- [{Event} is the best part of the term!|Yes! {Event}!] [Promise you'll come?|I've got a whole plan.]
- [Only a little longer till {event}.|I've been counting the days to {event}.] [I'm so excited.|Let's make it memorable.]

@rule school.event.low
on school
when school=event low=yes
opens comfort,invite,ask
- [{Event}...|Ugh, is that soon?] [I'm not really in the mood.|I don't know if I'll go.|Maybe if someone came with me...]
- [{Event} again...|I forgot about {event}.] [I don't really feel like it.|Maybe I'll stay home.]
- [Everyone's so excited about {event}.|{Event}, huh.] [I just can't get into it.|Wake me up when it's over.]

@rule school.event.club
on school
when school=event hasclub=yes
opens ask,praise,invite
- [The {club} is doing something for {event}.|We've been preparing for {event} at the {club}.] [Come see us?|It's a lot of work.|I'm kind of nervous.]
- [The {club} has a booth at {event}.|We're putting on a show at {event}.] [Stop by!|Wish us luck.]
- [{Event} means double practice at the {club}.|I'm in charge of something for the {club} at {event}.] [I'm exhausted.|Don't laugh if I mess up.]

@rule school.council
on school
when school=council
opens ask,agree,tease
- [The council race? {Eventline}.|Everyone's picking sides for the council.] [Who are you voting for?|It's getting intense.|I just want it to be over.]
- [Posters everywhere for the council race.|The council debate was something.] [Who are you backing?|Pretty heated.]
- [Council elections are a popularity contest.|I heard the council candidates are fighting.] [Change my mind.|Politics, even here.]

@rule school.project
on school
when school=project
opens ask,praise,invite
- [The club project? {Eventline}.|We're still working on the project.] [It's coming along.|We could use a hand, honestly.|I think it'll turn out well.]
- [The project is almost done.|The project's eating all our free time.] [Fingers crossed.|But it's worth it.]
- [We had a breakthrough on the project.|The project needs one more push.] [Finally.|Want to help?]

@rule school.exam
on school
when exam=yes
opens comfort,invite,ask
feel worried
- [Don't remind me about the exams.|Exams, exams, exams.] [Want to study together?|I'm so behind.|If I fail one more test...]
- [Exams are coming and my brain is empty.|I keep dreaming about the exams.] [Save me.|Bad dreams.]
- [Did you start studying for the exams?|Only a few days till the exams.] [Please say no.|I'm panicking.]

@rule school.cool
on school
when voice=cool|serious|proper
opens ask,agree
- [{Event}. It's well organized this year.|I've read the schedule for {event}.] [It should go smoothly.|Do you need the details?]
- [{Event}. I've planned accordingly.|I'm helping organize {event}.] [It won't be a problem.|Some of it, anyway.]
- [{Event} comes every year.|I'll attend {event}, of course.] [Nothing to get excited about.|It's expected.]

@rule school.genki
on school
when voice=genki|energetic|boyish|tough
opens invite,tease,ask
feel laugh
- [{Event}! I'm totally going to win!|{Event} is gonna be awesome!] [You'd better cheer for me!|Bet I beat you!]
- [{Event}! I can't sit still!|Let's go all out at {event}!] [It's gonna be epic!|You and me, team!]
- [I've been training for {event} all week!|{Event}! Finally!] [Watch me!|Let's goooo!]
